rota lap 4671, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels (law and boundary); read TAME_CORE, single-stranded, GAUGE_STYLE. Single-stranded named the fault exactly: one heading was carrying two questions, and a paragraph written to untangle it was carrying a third.
think Reds first. Cold roster 269 run, 264 green, 3 red. `stash_record` is the peer-owed `stash@{13}`; `standing_equipment` only reports the other two; `tracked_link` read red at 06s in the pass and GREEN on re-run at the same HEAD, so I record it as a red that does not reproduce rather than inventing a cause.
think My handoff owed %714's remainder -- `Line length <= 100` standing under **Enforced now**. The peer had already landed the census, so the row was answered. What stood unanswered was the heading itself, and the paragraph written beneath the table to explain it.
think Measured the paragraph rather than trusting it. It reads *eight lean on five tools a roster pass runs every lap*, written `20260911.112513`. Read `20260912` against the same two files: ten every lap, one on cadence, nine by hand. The round that wrote the sentence rostered two of the rows it was counting, so it was two short before the file was saved.
think Three more rows read `by hand` only because they name the bans scan alone while `tame_style_check` drives it every lap. Naming the driver in the row is the repair; a driver map inside the scan would put the relationship in a second file two readers could disagree about.
obs The durable move is a column, not a better paragraph. A count typed into prose is free by Gauge's fifth question, and this one proved it at one day's resolution.
obs `Enforced now` was two claims wearing one heading -- *has an instrument today* (true of all twenty) and *a lap will catch you* (true of thirteen). `Checkable today` keeps the first and the Runs column carries the second, so the contrast with the *Horizon* table below survives.
obs The pen's first draft entered the table at its first bold rule and would have dropped an unbolded row in silence. Anchored at the delimiter instead -- a population that can lose a member is the fault this family exists to catch.
obs The hot pass refused my own filing: `tool_letter_room` read `misfiled=3` because I filed all three files under `t` for TAME, the subject, where a letter room is decided by the file's own first sprig letter. Moved to `l`, seven citing files repointed, ceiling back to zero.
obs No REDS row could be booked: `reds_pin_capacity` reads `pin_deadlocked=1`, `rows_that_fit=0`, `pin_foldable_rows=0`. Keyed by its stamp, `20260912.011500`, per the derived-spine law.
